From 873e38ae07bc9473c7e895fde614f708b27691de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 08:15:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: himax-hx8279: drive reset and enable as outputs
 before toggling them

The reset and enable lines are requested GPIOD_ASIS so that a panel the
bootloader left running is not disturbed at probe, and the driver then
only ever calls gpiod_set_value() on them. That inherits whatever
direction the bootloader left. On gtaxlwifi RESX (gpd4-1) is left as an
input held high by its pull-up, and on the Samsung pinctrl a set_value on
an input pin writes DAT without touching CON: the reset the driver
believes it asserts in power_off() and releases in prepare() never
reaches the panel. The DriverIC is only ever reset by its own power-on
reset when the LCD rails come back, with RESX already high, which the
datasheet does not allow and which sometimes leaves the GOA timing in a
bad state: horizontal single-line stripes on a wake-up, worse on the
next one, seen three times on kernel #15-#17 with an otherwise identical
and error-free DSI sequence in dmesg.

power_off() is the first place the driver drives the lines after the
bootloader handoff, so set the direction there: gpiod_direction_output()
instead of gpiod_set_value(), for both lines. Every later set_value in
prepare(), including the reset pulse, then really toggles the pin. The
enable line is optional and a NULL descriptor is a no-op.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx8279.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx8279.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx8279.c
index 0413745076..d680d5ced6 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx8279.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx8279.c
@@ -920,9 +920,18 @@ static void hx8279_power_off(struct hx8279 *hx)
 	/* The DriverIC comes back on page 0 after a power cycle */
 	hx->last_page = 0;
 
-	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(hx->reset_gpio, 0);
+	/*
+	 * The lines are requested GPIOD_ASIS so that a panel left running
+	 * by the bootloader is not disturbed at probe. The direction is
+	 * therefore whatever the bootloader left: on gtaxlwifi RESX (gpd4-1)
+	 * is an input held high by its pull-up, and gpiod_set_value() on an
+	 * input pin never reaches the panel. This is the first time the
+	 * driver drives the lines, so make them outputs here; every later
+	 * gpiod_set_value() in prepare() then really toggles the pin.
+	 */
+	gpiod_direction_output(hx->reset_gpio, 0);
 	usleep_range(100, 500);
-	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(hx->enable_gpio, 0);
+	gpiod_direction_output(hx->enable_gpio, 0);
 	regulator_bulk_disable(ARRAY_SIZE(hx->vregs), hx->vregs);
 }
 
